## Plan

## Approach

Create a typed, immutable per-item adjudication engine over `voting.py`. Each family prepares its own item context, invokes the engine exactly once per ballot, then serializes the cached results into its existing classification TSV, ledger, score rows, tally table, and artifact files.

The engine owns shared policy evaluation only: vote-result selection from the supplied OOS context, neutral rescue, OOS fileability, score kind/result/weight, unique-finder eligibility, ledger outcome, reroute marker, agreement inputs, and artifact-routing decisions. Family adapters retain parsing inputs, security probes, row schemas, tuple shapes, wrappers, paths, numbering, and error translation.

Preserve all CLI entry points, status KVs, headers, paths, output bytes, and caller contracts. Require a net production-line reduction.

